# WORKROOM-2T fix: pre-measured LazyVStack for DiffViewer

## Root cause recap (unchanged from the brief, confirmed against current source)

`macapp/WorkroomApp/Views/DiffViewer.swift:381-436` (`unifiedBody`/`sideBySideBody`) renders every diff line in an eager `VStack` specifically because `styledText` (line 604) uses `.fixedSize(horizontal: false, vertical: true)` and a naive `LazyVStack` would cache a wrong height for a not-yet-materialized wrapping row. Each row is its own accessibility leaf (`lineRow` line 542-543, `sideCell` line 496-498), so a near-cap (~2000-line) diff puts ~2000 nodes in the tree that `ResponderNode.visitFocusResponders` walks on every `NSHostingView.layout` pass — the confirmed Sentry stack. Fix: pre-measure real wrapped heights, then use a genuine `LazyVStack` with explicit per-row frame heights.

---

## Phase 0 — Fidelity go/no-go benchmark (build before touching `DiffViewer.swift`)

This is the actual risk in this plan — not measurement speed, but whether `NSLayoutManager`'s wrap points agree with SwiftUI `Text`'s. A 1pt-short measurement means `.frame` clips or overdraws the last visual line — a **persistent, silent** bug, strictly worse than the blank band this fix removes. The live repro was a CSS file; if it was minified, its lines are long unbroken tokens, exactly where word-wrap vs. character-wrap fallback diverges hardest (a whole-line disagreement, not fractional).

**New test file:** `macapp/WorkroomAppTests/DiffLineMetricsFidelityTests.swift`

- Adversarial fixture strings: a ~5000-char no-whitespace token (simulates minified CSS), a line with tabs, a line with CJK/emoji, and a line hand-tuned to land within ~2pt of a wrap boundary at a fixed test width.
- Host a small `NSHostingView`/`NSWindow` at a fixed width containing `Text` rows built exactly like `styledText` (same font, same `.fixedSize(horizontal: false, vertical: true)`), using the `host()`/`settle()` pattern from `HistoryRowInvalidationTests.swift`/`PaneRenderingTests.swift`.
- Read back each row's real laid-out height (e.g. via `.onGeometryChange`/a `PreferenceKey` capturing height into an array, read after `settle()`).
- Compare against `DiffLineMetrics.Session.height(of:)` for the same strings/width/font.
- **Go:** heights agree within a small tolerance (~1pt) on every case, including the unbreakable-token case (same line count, not 1-vs-20). **No-go:** any case disagrees by more than a fraction of a point, or the unbreakable-token case disagrees in line count — that's the explicit trigger to stop and reconsider option (b) (AppKit-hosted virtualized control) rather than shipping a wrong-height cache. Surface this decision to the user before proceeding either way.
- Also use this phase to empirically pin: whether the `ScrollView`'s scroller consumes width (overlay scrollers shouldn't, but verify), and whether `NSLayoutManager` measurement gives correct results when run off-main (relevant if the recompute is later moved to `Task.detached`).

