## 1. New file: `macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/DiffLineMetrics.swift`

Pure measurement logic, no SwiftUI/DiffViewer dependency beyond `UnifiedDiff`.

```swift
enum DiffLineMetrics {
  enum LayoutMode: Equatable { case unified, sideBySide }

  struct Cache: Equatable {
    let mode: LayoutMode
    let rows: [[CGFloat]]   // index-aligned with diff.hunks[i].lines (unified) or sbsRows.rows[i] (sideBySide)
  }

  /// Resolves a concrete NSFont that tracks Dynamic Type for the `.callout` style `styledText` uses.
  static func measurementFont() -> NSFont {
    NSFont.monospacedSystemFont(
      ofSize: NSFont.preferredFont(forTextStyle: .callout).pointSize, weight: .regular)
  }

  /// Content width available to the TEXT, given DiffViewer's own chrome widths (passed in, never
  /// duplicated here — `DiffViewer.gutterWidth`/`sideGutterWidth` stay the single source of truth).
  static func textWidth(
    contentWidth: CGFloat, mode: LayoutMode,
    unifiedChrome: CGFloat, sideBySideChromePerColumn: CGFloat, dividerWidth: CGFloat
  ) -> CGFloat { ... }

  /// One NSTextStorage/NSLayoutManager/NSTextContainer triple, reused across every line of one
  /// measurement pass by swapping text via `replaceCharacters` — NOT allocated per line (perf
  /// requirement: 2000 fresh stacks risked reintroducing a smaller hang during diff load).
  final class Session {
    init(font: NSFont, width: CGFloat)
    /// Applies the SAME empty-line substitution `styledText` uses (blank line → " ", not "").
    func height(of text: String) -> CGFloat
  }

  static func unifiedHeights(
    for diff: UnifiedDiff, contentWidth: CGFloat, font: NSFont,
    unifiedChrome: CGFloat, rowVerticalPadding: CGFloat
  ) -> [[CGFloat]]

  static func sideBySideHeights(
    for rows: [[UnifiedDiff.SideBySideRow]], contentWidth: CGFloat, font: NSFont,
    sideBySideChromePerColumn: CGFloat, dividerWidth: CGFloat, rowVerticalPadding: CGFloat
  ) -> [[CGFloat]]   // per row: ceil(max(leftHeight, rightHeight)) + rowVerticalPadding
}
```

**`Session` internals** (the concrete answer to "reuse one `NSLayoutManager` stack"): `container.lineFragmentPadding = 0` (AppKit defaults to 5pt, which SwiftUI `Text` doesn't have — must zero it for width accuracy); container size set **once** at `init` (width fixed for the session's lifetime, not per line); no `widthTracksTextView` (no text view exists — the earlier `CodeTextView.swift` precedent needs it because it drives a real `NSTextView`, this doesn't). Each `height(of:)` call does `storage.replaceCharacters` then **re-applies `.font` and an explicit `NSParagraphStyle`** (`lineBreakMode = .byWordWrapping`) over the full current length — `replaceCharacters` can drop attributes on the replaced range, and a measurement at the wrong font/break-mode is a silent wrong answer. Height comes from `layoutManager.usedRect(for: container).height` after `layoutManager.ensureLayout(for: container)` — no per-glyph walk needed.

Uses **real text layout**, not character-count arithmetic: diff content is arbitrary source code that may contain tabs and CJK/emoji, and a monospaced font doesn't give those the same advance width as a plain ASCII character — arithmetic estimation would be wrong for exactly the content most likely to appear in real code (deliberately rejected per the brief).

